/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T ( Blood banks are essential for collecting, storing, and distributing blood to patients in need. They classify donated blood by type, ensure its quality, and manage inventory. Traditional manual systems are time-consuming and inefficient in tracking blood quality and donor information. The Blood Bank Management System aims to automate these processes, providing an effective, time-efficient, and cost-effective solution that reduces manpower requirements.)
/E ( Blood banks are essential for collecting, storing, and distributing blood to patients in need. They classify donated blood by type, ensure its quality, and manage inventory. Traditional manual systems are time-consuming and inefficient in tracking blood quality and donor information. The Blood Bank Management System aims to automate these processes, providing an effective, time-efficient, and cost-effective solution that reduces manpower requirements.)
